Description: cap parallel make jobs on amd64 to avoid cc1plus OOM
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
Bug-Athena: Surfaced 2026-05-15 after the DEBIAN_RUST_LTO=-Clto=off
 patch (9001) successfully unblocked the gkrust OOM but exposed a
 second, distinct OOM during C++ compile.  Failure-mode in the build
 log:
 .
   g++-11: fatal error: Killed signal terminated program cc1plus
   compilation terminated.
   make[5]: *** [config/rules.mk:674: UnifiedBindings26.o] Error 1
 .
 Same memory-pressure root cause, different process getting OOM-killed.
 Mozilla's `Unified_cpp_*.cpp` / `UnifiedBindings*.cpp` are auto-
 generated concatenations of many source files into a single
 compilation unit (the "unified build" technique — reduces header-parse
 overhead, but each .cpp becomes a 10-50k LoC monster).  cc1plus's
 peak resident set on these is ~3 GB; with `dh_auto_build --parallel`
 falling back to `nproc` (= 8 on this host), 8 concurrent cc1plus
 reach ~24 GB.  Combined with the parallel gkrust rustc still running
 (now ~2-3 GB with -Clto=off, was ~6-8 GB with -Clto), total memory
 demand on a 16 GB host saturates and the kernel OOM-killer fires.
 .
 PRIOR ATTEMPT (commit 103557f, this same patch's earlier shape)
 exported `DEB_BUILD_OPTION_PARALLEL=1` and had NO effect — the build
 still ran `make -j8` and cc1plus OOM'd identically.  Root cause:
 wrong env var.  `dh_auto_build`'s parallelism comes from debhelper's
 `Dh_Lib::get_buildoption('parallel')`, which reads `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS`
 (the canonical input string — same one that holds `nodoc nocheck`)
 and parses `parallel=N` out of it.  Verbatim from
 debhelper's lib/Debian/Debhelper/Dh_Lib.pm:
 .
   sub get_buildoption {
       my ($wanted, $default) = @_;
       return $default if not exists($ENV{DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS});
       foreach my $opt (split(/\s+/, $ENV{DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS})) {
           if ($opt =~ /^parallel=(-?\d+)$/ && $wanted eq 'parallel') {
               return $1;
           }
           ...
 .
 `DEB_BUILD_OPTION_PARALLEL` is a related-but-different env var
 dpkg-buildpackage sometimes pre-populates as a convenience for raw
 makefile recipes that want an integer; dh_auto_build does NOT read
 it.  The two names are confusingly similar; this is the second
 time the conflation has bitten this session.
 .
 Right fix: mutate DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS itself in debian/rules.  Append
 `parallel=1` so dh_auto_build's get_buildoption returns 1, capping
 the make invocation to `make -j1`.  Arch-gated on amd64 to mirror
 the matching DEBIAN_RUST_LTO block just above.
 .
 Memory math on a 16 GB host:
 .
   At -j1: 1 × ~3 GB cc1plus + ~3 GB gkrust + ~1-2 GB shell/parents
           = ~7 GB peak.  Comfortable headroom.
   At -j2: 2 × ~3 GB cc1plus + ~3 GB gkrust = ~10 GB peak.  Likely
           safe but less margin.
   At -j8: 8 × ~3 GB cc1plus + ~3 GB gkrust = ~27 GB peak.  OOMs.
 .
 Trade-off: -j1 is ~6-8x slower than -j8 for the C++ portion (gkrust
 is already a single rustc, so the Rust phase is unaffected).  Total
 firefox-esr wall-clock at -j1 is ~3-5 hours vs ~30-45 min at -j8 —
 but the -j8 build OOMs and produces nothing.  Slow + working beats
 fast + broken.
 .
 Verification this time: the `parallel=N` knob is the canonical
 Debian-policy input.  Reference: Debian Policy 4.9.1.  Verbatim
 in debhelper's get_buildoption — directly cited above.  In
 production, dh_auto_build's chosen `make -jN` will be visible in
 the build log; expected pattern is `make -j1` instead of `make -j8`.
 If a future run shows `make -j2` or higher despite this patch,
 either dpkg-buildpackage stripped the appended value (it shouldn't —
 the env var is propagated verbatim) or another mechanism is at
 work and this patch needs another round.
 .
 Pairs with 9001 (DEBIAN_RUST_LTO=-Clto=off).  Both apply on amd64.
 Mirrors the existing armhf and s390x arch-gated memory-budget
 patterns in upstream Debian's debian/rules.
 .
 Revert this patch only when paired with confirmation that the
 build host has ≥ ~24 GB RAM headroom, OR when [Source] parallelism
 in build.conf is dropped to 1 globally (which already serialises
 rust+c++ across the pipeline so per-package -j8 is fine).
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -251,6 +251,15 @@ endif
 ifeq (amd64,$(DEB_BUILD_ARCH))
 export DEBIAN_RUST_LTO=-Clto=off
 endif
+# Athena amd64: build hosts may have ~16 GB RAM.  Mozilla's
+# UnifiedBindings*.cpp files compile at ~3 GB peak per cc1plus; default
+# -j8 + parallel gkrust together exceed the OOM threshold.  Append
+# parallel=1 to DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS so dh_auto_build's get_buildoption()
+# reads it (DEB_BUILD_OPTION_PARALLEL is NOT what dh_auto_build reads —
+# debhelper parses DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS directly).
+ifeq (amd64,$(DEB_BUILD_ARCH))
+export DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS := $(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS) parallel=1
+endif
 
 stamps/build-$(PRODUCT):: stamps/configure-check-$(PRODUCT)
 	+dh_auto_build --parallel --builddirectory=build-$(PRODUCT)
